cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Donghyunsam (동현삼): a single-player Three Kingdoms strategy simulation game on a map of 41 provinces with hex battles, with starting values and rule numbers set through the esoteric language Donghyun-lang"
type: software
version: "0.08"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24106052"
date-released: "2026-11-14"
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Dong Hyun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9883-0229"
    affiliation: "Inha University College of Medicine"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Raspberry-Kim/donghyun-lab16"
url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lab16/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyunsam is a browser-based, noncommercial toy that follows only the
  broad frame of Romance of the Three Kingdoms II (Koei, 1989): the player
  picks one of nine rulers on a node map of 41 provinces of late Han China
  and gives one order per province per month (develop farmland, draft, move,
  search, invade, relief, alliance). A province with no officer becomes
  vacant land that an officer can occupy by moving in. An invasion opens a 10x10 hex battlefield with terrain
  movement costs and defence modifiers; the other rulers are played by a
  simple priority-based AI. Starting values, rule numbers, the victory
  condition and time limit are set through a program written in the esoteric
  programming language Donghyun-lang, whose integer output is read as pairs
  of setting number and value by a shared adapter. The game runs on a small
  common engine (fixed 60-tick loop, calendar, square and hex grids with A*
  path finding, tile map renderer, scene stack) written in HTML5 Canvas and
  vanilla JavaScript and shared with Donghyunhang. The land and sea tiles
  are derived from Natural Earth 110m land data (public domain); province
  adjacency and all numbers are test values chosen for this work and were
  not checked against the original game. No graphic, sound, text, number or
  code of the original game is used or extracted. Romance of the Three
  Kingdoms is a series of Koei Tecmo Games; this work is unaffiliated. Input
  is keyboard, mouse or touch, with a fullscreen mode; the whole game can be
  played from the keyboard alone. A game can be saved by hand to three
  browser slots or to a .dhsave file and loaded back, together with the
  applied settings, the calendar and the random-number state. Sound effects
  are synthesized in the browser with the Web Audio API (no audio files)
  and can be switched off with a header button or the M key. A start card
  waits on the map until the player presses Sortie. The map shades the sea
  in three depths by distance from shore and tints land with the colour of
  the nearest ruler. The MIT
  license applies to the Donghyunsam code and documentation; the page fonts
  are under the SIL Open Font License. See LICENSE and CREDITS.md.
keywords:
  - turn-based strategy
  - strategy simulation game
  - Romance of the Three Kingdoms
  - hex grid
  - esoteric programming language
  - JavaScript
